  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 vs config_002 (pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.591, suggesting scvi improves performance by ~0.06. However, this comparison is confounded because both use multiprofile+avgpool. The singleprofile PCA baseline (config_001) is 0.485. Uncertainty: Is the scvi improvement driven by the encoder itself or by an interaction with multiprofile? config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) directly isolates the encoder effect by changing only the RNA encoder relative to config_001. If scvi-singleprofile substantially exceeds 0.485, the encoder matters independently and we should prioritize encoder choice in multimodal designs. If it remains near 0.485, the gain is profile-interaction-driven, shifting focus to aggregation. This single-variable comparison is the most efficient way to reduce uncertainty about a core design axis before committing budget to more complex multimodal configurations."
}

